# Tests of chat.kkl, run in examples/ (see examples/README.md). demo runs
# the server in a worker and two clients over inproc:// endpoints; each
# step waits for what it broadcasts, so the output is always the same. A
# server and clients in several processes cannot be run from here.

$ demo
ann and bob hear the heartbeat
[ann, bob] * ann joined
[ann, bob] * bob joined
[ann, bob] ann: hi bob
[ann, bob] bob: hi ann, the disk is full again
ann: ann is already here
ann: carol has not joined
ann: unknown request dance
status: 2 here (ann, bob), 2 said
[ann, bob] * bob left
stop: the server stops
ann: no heartbeat for 0.5 s: the server is gone
the server's log, until it stopped after 5 broadcasts:
  serving inproc://chat and inproc://chat-pub
  * ann joined
  * bob joined
  ann: hi bob
  bob: hi ann, the disk is full again
  * bob left

$ talk tcp://localhost:5555
! chat: wrong command line: talk tcp://localhost:5555
! usage: chat server [-beat S] endpoint pub-endpoint | client endpoint name [message ...] | status endpoint | stop endpoint | demo
exit 2

$ status
! chat: wrong command line: status
! usage: chat server [-beat S] endpoint pub-endpoint | client endpoint name [message ...] | status endpoint | stop endpoint | demo
exit 2

$ client tcp://localhost:5555
! chat: client needs an endpoint and a name
! usage: chat server [-beat S] endpoint pub-endpoint | client endpoint name [message ...] | status endpoint | stop endpoint | demo
exit 2

$ server tcp://*:5555
! chat: server needs an endpoint and a pub-endpoint
! usage: chat server [-beat S] endpoint pub-endpoint | client endpoint name [message ...] | status endpoint | stop endpoint | demo
exit 2

$ server -beat soon tcp://*:5555 tcp://*:5556
! chat: -beat takes 0.01 to 3600 seconds
! usage: chat server [-beat S] endpoint pub-endpoint | client endpoint name [message ...] | status endpoint | stop endpoint | demo
exit 2

$ server localhost:5555 tcp://127.0.0.1:0
! chat: zmq::Socket::bind: "localhost:5555" is not an endpoint such as "tcp://localhost:5555"
exit 1
